{
  "assessment_scope": "Governed final Verify of 2026-09-15-refine-skills-and-retire-stale-support at 20d1ecd170d6031f9081fbc4a015dd5194e28609 against original main 3c4985f80b242a295116880a5aee9cbbf47b12b0. Assesses exact approved proposal, four Designs, stable plan, complete final diff, all19 skill packages, complete script/test/fixture/caller population, candidate parity, current requirement coverage, review closeout and Git/PR handoff. This is distinct from independent final Code Review.",
  "change_id": "2026-09-15-refine-skills-and-retire-stale-support",
  "changes": [
    "Five skill entrypoints now trigger complete conditional recording resources; reader validation and negative cases protect missing, wrong, escaped and incomplete guidance. Current owner descriptions, plan navigation, PR rationale and Claude examples are reconciled.",
    "The obsolete Python query shim, exclusive checks and orphan parser are retired together. Deleted/renamed paths still select surviving checks; current record interfaces preserve invalid-input, identity, privacy and no-mutation boundaries.",
    "All19 skill packages and the full allocated support population have evidence-backed retain/refine/retire dispositions. Dead fixture APIs, self-fulfilling assertions, duplicate cases and obsolete historical PR budget support are removed while historical assessment records remain unchanged.",
    "The existing Verify closed-vocabulary test now proves its current v3 control succeeds before unknown outcome rejection. Real public process, persistence/recovery, archive/install and release protections remain."
  ],
