  "limitations": [
    "Hosted CI has not yet been observed for the submitted head. All pass claims here are local direct, selected or isolated candidate checks.",
    "The pre-existing generated-only adapter-support Design/source migration remains incomplete: live dist/adapters support files/readers are retained because changing build/release defaults is outside this approved maintenance scope.",
    "Candidate validation used temporary clean installs and qualification label v1.0.0. No public release, active user installation, merge or publication was performed or authorized.",
    "Skill review establishes inspected reading paths and package integrity, not universal agent behavior, benchmarked token savings or timing guarantees."
  ],
  "outcome": "success",
  "rationale": [
    "SKL-SR-33–35 and HAND-SR-04 are supported by complete package/reading-path assessment, independent normal/governed/late/failure review, selected-resource negatives and actual canonical/archive/install parity. Simplification changes navigation without transferring substantive duties or authorizing lifecycle actions.",
    "VAL-SR-29–31 and CLI-SR-31 are supported by full body/caller/discovery inventories, coupled query retirement, actual Git deletion/rename and mixed unknown-path proof, and explicit replacement or retirement reasons. Counts document population only; independent failure observations justify retained protection.",
    "All four milestone reviews and the fresh independent final whole-change review approve the exact assessed scope. The earlier Design decision-ID collision is reporter-resolved and independently rereviewed; no open material finding or blocker remains. Governing subject identities are unchanged from accepted approvals.",
    "Direct suites, corrected fail-first control, generator parity, local selection and immutable original-base PR/main checks pass. Main reports1034 checks; current package suite418. Integrated gates ran at7bab3b1fd7ee4ca27a967013f7358c5349ac640c; later changes are attributable owning validation/review/workflow evidence only, with no changed engineering input.",
    "Fresh M3 Codex/Claude candidates retain all138 canonical members across19skills and complete triggered resources; an independent final comparator reconfirmed exact declared transforms and current Claude /design guidance. M4 changed tests/support only, so candidate inputs remain identical.",
    "Git base/head/merge-base and remote identities are resolved; no unrelated working-tree changes or remote branch divergence exists. Current committed record validation and diff checks support the evidence-only suffix. This establishes branch readiness, leaving PR creation and hosted CI to their respective owners."
  ],
